    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.snippets\n\n### Description\n\nis there a similar command in ` mini.snippets` as `require(\"luasnip\").snip_expand()` in `luasnip` to e.g. trigger a snippet by a keymap?\n\n```lua\nvim.keymap.set(\"i\", <keyboard_keys>, function()\n\trequire(\"luasnip\").snip_expand(require(\"keymap_snippets\")[<snippet_key>])\nend)\n```\n\nIf not, could it be added to `mini.snippets`?",
