    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Yes, there is. In 'mini.snippets' this process is called \"inserting snippet\" (opposite to \"expanding\" which also includes computing all available snippets at the context and matching against text at cursor).\n\nThe default one is [`default_insert()`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/d90adc96b68b310cf17d8ebcc8e2e4626c6bb8cc/doc/mini-snippets.txt#L1007), while the plugins should [first try to use `MiniSnippets.config.expand.insert`](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/d90adc96b68b310cf17d8ebcc8e2e4626c6bb8cc/doc/mini-snippets.txt#L526-L527) to respect changes user might have made.",
            "created_at": "2025-05-26T19:20:52Z",
